---
import WikiLayout from '../../layouts/WikiLayout.astro';
import DevlogNav from '../../components/DevlogNav.astro';
---
<WikiLayout
  title="Below Deck: October 2026"
  section="devlog"
  description="Official production kickoff with the full team, Quest Unplayed podcast appearance, welcoming Erin and Sarah to sound crew, and heading to MIGS in Montreal."
  ogImage="/images/devlog/october-2026/thumbnail.png"
>
  <div class="wiki-content devlog-entry">

    <div class="entry-meta">
      <a href="/devlog" class="back-link">&larr; All Devlogs</a>
      <span class="entry-date">October 2026</span>
    </div>

    <h1>Official production kickoff 🏴‍☠️ | October 2026</h1>

    <p>Ahoy crew, welcome below deck!</p>

    <p>So I think this might be the first month in over two years of newsletters that I've been late to get the email out. You'd think with me going full time that I'd be flush with hours to spend crafting cool communications and marketing material&hellip; turns out I'm not.</p>

    <p>My excuses for not getting my homework in on time? I'm a week out from heading to Canada to pitch at MIGS, my third child is less than 2 months old and we're still in the sleep deprived phase, and then last week my computer's power supply died and my 3 year old ended up in the emergency room with a head bump. It's been a wild start!</p>

    <h2>Setting sail again with the full team</h2>

    <p>The Cass Bay Games team have officially kicked off production, and we are drawing to the end of our second fortnightly sprint. So far the art crew have been very busy, with Simon reworking the combat HUD, and Nik adding extra character sprites to increase the impact and fidelity of combat. The sound crew have been auditing our existing sound processes and reworking our pipeline for a really strong foundation to build on going forward. And I myself have been busy implementing the new art systems, and developing our pitch for when I travel to Canada.</p>

    <img src="/images/devlog/october-2026/combat.gif" alt="Combat screenshot showing new HUD and character sprites" class="devlog-img" />

    <h2>Davy Jones' Deckhand on the Quest Unplayed podcast</h2>

    <p>I had the pleasure of being a guest on the Quest Unplayed podcast. I dressed for the occasion and overshared about my personal journey getting into game development.</p>

    <img src="/images/devlog/october-2026/quest-unplayed.png" alt="Quest Unplayed podcast - Chapter 102: You have never seen a deckbuilder like this" class="devlog-img" />

    <p>You can watch the interview on <a href="https://youtu.be/J-aMyJSoylc" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><b>YouTube</b></a> or <a href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/4uCXbXnv1fKuIC52hllnia" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><b>Spotify</b></a>.</p>

    <h2>Welcoming Erin and Sarah to the team (officially)</h2>

    <p>I'm very excited to announce we have added two new members to the development crew, Erin and Sarah! Both of these talented sound designers did some internship hours with us as part of their master's studies, and we're stoked to now bring them on in a more official capacity to continue their awesome sound work for Davy Jones' Deckhand.</p>

    <img src="/images/devlog/october-2026/sound-crew.png" alt="Sound crew - Erin and Sarah" class="devlog-img" />

    <h2>Taking Deckhand on another overseas voyage!</h2>

    <img src="/images/devlog/october-2026/migs.png" alt="See you in Montreal - MIGS 2026, 10-11 November" class="devlog-img" />

    <p>I'm heading to the Montreal International Games Summit with the CODE NZ cohort. I'll be looking for publishing partners/project-based investors for the game. With our recent CODE StartUp grant we are in full production mode for the next 13 months, but we're still seeking a publisher or project-based investor who can invest in our marketing, and provide finishing funds. I fly 30+ hours on Sunday, spend 3 nights in Canada, then straight back home. This is the way when juggling game business ambition with busy family life!</p>

    <p>I look forward to returning from the big trip and settling into more of a development flow.</p>

    <p>Thanks for being here!<br /><b>Ben</b></p>

    <DevlogNav currentSlug="october-2026" />

  </div>
</WikiLayout>

<style>
  .devlog-entry {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--ocean);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--gold-dark);
  }

  .entry-date {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .devlog-img {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }

  .img-pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }

  .img-pair .devlog-img {
    margin: 0;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  li a {
    color: var(--gold);
  }
</style>
